Personal balance sheets list assets and debts; income statements track receipts and spending.|Assets ₹20 lakh less debts ₹8 lakh gives net worth ₹12 lakh.|Borrowing and retaining ₹2 lakh cash initially changes net worth by…?|Zero|+₹2 lakh|−₹2 lakh
Budgets allocate income across needs, goals, and discretionary spending; tracking tests reality.|Income ₹50,000 less spending ₹40,000 leaves ₹10,000 monthly saving.|A sustainable plan should include…?|Irregular expenses and actual behaviour|Only last week's spending|Only desired savings
Emergency funds provide accessible reserves for shocks; appropriate size depends on obligations and income stability.|Essential costs ₹30,000 monthly imply ₹180,000 for an assumed six-month buffer.|Six months is a universal rule for everyone?|No|Yes|Only for employees
Debt management compares rates, terms, penalties, and liquidity; credit scores summarise specific repayment information.|A high-cost revolving balance competes with discretionary investing.|A high score guarantees affordable borrowing?|No|Yes|Only for salaried borrowers
Education, vehicle, and housing loans differ in collateral, benefits, term, and repayment flexibility.|A lower monthly payment can reflect a longer term and greater total interest.|Choose only by monthly instalment?|No|Yes|Only for mortgages
Financial goals specify amount, date, inflation, and priority; savings plans connect contributions with assumed returns.|A goal costing ₹100 now at 5% inflation costs about ₹127.63 in five years.|Ignoring inflation can understate…?|Required future savings|Current debt balance|Current income tax
Insurance needs analysis matches protection to dependants, debts, health exposure, and existing resources.|Outstanding obligations exceed assets available to dependants.|Protection needs depend only on income multiples?|No|Yes|Only for term insurance
Personal allocation matches goals, horizon, capacity, liquidity, and diversification.|Near-term rent cash and long-term retirement savings have different constraints.|Use one identical portfolio for all goals automatically?|No|Yes|Only for beginners
Tax efficiency compares after-tax outcomes within applicable rules without letting tax benefits dominate suitability.|A deductible product charges high fees and restricts access.|A tax deduction alone proves suitability?|No|Yes|Only for retirement
Retirement plans estimate spending, inflation, longevity, portfolio outcomes, and withdrawal rules.|Early market losses during withdrawals can deplete assets disproportionately.|This is…?|Sequence-of-returns risk|Only average-return risk|Guaranteed recovery
Inflation reduces purchasing power; longevity extends the period resources must support.|Fixed nominal income buys less when living costs rise.|A high nominal balance guarantees preserved purchasing power?|No|Yes|Only after retirement
Stock compensation combines employment and investment exposure; vesting, exercise, taxes, and concentration matter.|Salary and a large shareholding depend on the same employer.|This raises…?|Concentrated economic exposure|Automatic diversification|Guaranteed liquidity
Buy-versus-rent compares total costs, flexibility, financing, and alternative investment opportunities.|Ownership adds maintenance, taxes, transaction costs, and foregone investment returns.|Mortgage payment alone captures ownership cost?|No|Yes|Only in one city
Family planning coordinates shared goals, dependants, contingencies, and decision responsibilities.|A single earner's interruption affects several dependants.|Planning should include…?|Resilience and agreed priorities|Only the earner's goals|Only investment returns
Estate tools organise ownership transfer; nominations, wills, and trusts have jurisdiction-specific legal effects.|An account nomination and a will may serve different functions.|A nominee is universally the final beneficial owner?|No|Yes|Only for bank accounts
Wealth preservation considers taxes, concentration, governance, heirs, and transfer costs.|A family holds nearly all wealth in one illiquid business.|Preservation planning should address…?|Liquidity and concentration|Only historical valuation|Only family size
Scams exploit urgency, unrealistic promises, impersonation, and weak verification.|An unsolicited offer promises high guaranteed returns and demands immediate payment.|Best first action?|Independently verify identity and claims|Pay before the deadline|Share credentials for verification
Adviser selection examines competence, duties, fees, incentives, and conflicts.|Commission-linked compensation can influence product recommendations.|Disclosure alone makes every conflict harmless?|No|Yes|Only for licensed advisers
